174
00:07:42,920 --> 00:07:47,340
Although fiction, by definition, is made up, it must be believable to succeed.

175
00:07:47,960 --> 00:07:53,660
Even fantasies and science fiction books must make sense to keep the reader willingly suspending disbelief.

176
00:07:54,100 --> 00:07:55,760
That's where research comes in.

177
00:07:56,560 --> 00:07:59,660
Specific factual detail adds flavor.

178
00:07:59,680 --> 00:08:00,780
And authenticity.

179
00:08:01,540 --> 00:08:07,640
You get geographical, cultural, or technological details wrong and your reader loses interest in your story.

180
00:08:08,300 --> 00:08:09,680
So here are some research resources.

181
00:08:11,080 --> 00:08:11,640
Atlases.

182
00:08:12,240 --> 00:08:13,180
World Almanacs.

183
00:08:14,060 --> 00:08:14,840
Encyclopedias.

184
00:08:15,540 --> 00:08:16,160
YouTube.

185
00:08:17,000 --> 00:08:17,700
Thesauri.

186
00:08:18,520 --> 00:08:22,140
Interviews, whether in person, by Skype, or by phone.

187
00:08:23,080 --> 00:08:26,040
Google and similar search engines.

188
00:08:27,040 --> 00:08:29,360
Never shortchange the research process.

189
00:08:29,680 --> 00:08:34,220
Also be careful not to overload your story with every esoteric fact you've learned.

190
00:08:34,960 --> 00:08:37,440
Add specifics the way you season food.

191
00:08:37,960 --> 00:08:39,560
Research adds flavor.

192
00:08:39,680 --> 00:08:41,080
It's not the main course.

193
00:08:41,620 --> 00:08:43,720
Your story is the main course.

194
00:08:44,940 --> 00:08:48,880
